{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795367541,"nonce":"vlB484K0osxjMB4fjmFLel83q4k=","message":"Found while auditing the plugin for step 4 of 61fbc22: thread_spawn_boxed takes a DynamicBox with Box::from_raw and lets the Box drop at the end of the call. A box that the host hands to a plugin is a block of the program's heap. The host makes it with DynamicBox::into_raw or box_on_heap and releases it with free_raw. Dropping it as a Rust Box returns a heap block to the system allocator. With the host allocator installed, that is undefined behavior. The fix is to call free on the payload and then DynamicBox::free_raw on the box. It is not changed in 2c6bcbcb.","files":null}]}